From: Ryan Walklin <ryan@testtoast.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] bus: sun50i: add DE33 compatible string to the DE2 bus driver
Upstream-Status: Submitted <https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-kernel/20250216092827.15444-1-ryan@testtoast.com/>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Walklin <ryan@testtoast.com>

The Allwinner H616/H700 DE33 display-engine bus block is register-
compatible with the A64 DE2 bus. Bind it so the display_clocks and
mixer0 children probe.

Squeezebox OOT note (WP3 panel): unchanged port of lore patch 1/8 to
linux v7.3.4 (context still applies verbatim). Validated: kernel DTB
build + sun50i-de2 cross-compile; hardware probe still gated. See
docs/test-results/wp3-panel.md.

--- a/drivers/bus/sun50i-de2.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/sun50i-de2.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 
 static const struct of_device_id sun50i_de2_bus_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-a64-de2", },
+	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-de33", },
 	{ /* sentinel */ }
 };
 
